1
00:00:01,550 --> 00:00:03,841
Hi, we’re Team AgriCan. This is AgriGenesis AI,

2
00:00:03,861 --> 00:00:07,520
for the Sustainability track, and Accessibility and Inclusion.

3
00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:11,322
By 2033, 280k acres of Nova Scotia farmland will change hands,

4
00:00:11,342 --> 00:00:15,340
and almost 36 percent of farmers have no successor.

5
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:19,764
Meet Sam. Sam just bought 98 acres near Pugwash, but has no idea what to grow,

6
00:00:19,784 --> 00:00:23,220
what the weather can do, or how to care for crops.

7
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:27,810
AgriGenesis AI gives Sam three features with many tools inside.

8
00:00:27,830 --> 00:00:30,860
Free, and always real, official data.

9
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:35,424
Feature 1, Plan Farm. Sam types the PID from the property tax notice.

10
00:00:35,444 --> 00:00:38,160
An address or a photo works too.

11
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:44,300
The boundary loads from the Nova Scotia property registry: 98 acres.

12
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:49,090
Sam’s goals: earn income, new to farming, under 5,000 dollars, and part-time.

13
00:00:50,130 --> 00:00:54,350
The agent pulls real frost, soil, slope, satellite and price data.

14
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:58,536
Sam’s land: 156 frost-free days, acidic sandy loam soil,

15
00:00:58,556 --> 00:01:01,710
gentle ground, and 85% already open farmland.

16
00:01:01,730 --> 00:01:04,954
What Sam can plant: potatoes, strawberries and sweet corn,

17
00:01:04,974 --> 00:01:07,770
all good fits, on small starter plots.

18
00:01:07,790 --> 00:01:11,540
Sam gets the first steps to do, in order, starting with a soil test,

19
00:01:12,020 --> 00:01:15,120
and a 12-month calendar of what to do each month.

20
00:01:16,170 --> 00:01:21,652
Income uses real Statistics Canada prices: strawberries could bring about $4,100 a year,

21
00:01:21,672 --> 00:01:25,540
about $2,100 of it profit, and sweet corn about $2,800.

22
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:28,294
And who to contact: the Farm Loan Board for land,

23
00:01:28,314 --> 00:01:33,150
Perennia for crop advice, and the Federation of Agriculture for succession.

24
00:01:33,170 --> 00:01:36,082
The agent fact-checks its own plan, 7 of 7 passed,

25
00:01:36,102 --> 00:01:39,400
and gives a sustainability score: 72, grade B.

26
00:01:39,810 --> 00:01:47,350
Feature 2, Climate Risk. Sam has a plan now, but one bad summer can wipe out the first harvest.

27
00:01:47,370 --> 00:01:51,770
So Sam checks strawberries on this land, looking back at last July.

28
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:56,870
It pulls that month’s real weather and NASA satellite data.

29
00:01:59,250 --> 00:02:04,890
Risk 36 out of 100, moderate: 32 percent heat stress and 33 percent drought.

30
00:02:04,910 --> 00:02:10,220
The AI explains what that means, and how to prepare next summer, like watering.

31
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:16,410
And for right now, it suggests what Sam can plant: garlic, winter rye and crimson clover.

32
00:02:16,430 --> 00:02:21,260
Feature 3, Crop Care, for the whole season. Sam’s plan carries over here too.

33
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:26,220
In July, Sam spots a sick potato leaf and uploads a photo.

34
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:33,220
The AI names likely causes and treatments, and says to confirm with an advisor.

35
00:02:34,530 --> 00:02:39,120
Its 7-day forecast for Sam’s field helps Sam plan the week’s work.

36
00:02:39,140 --> 00:02:44,780
It also shows the money for each crop from Statistics Canada, and AI tips to raise the yield.

37
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:50,690
And a farm assistant answers Sam’s questions from Sam’s own verified facts.

38
00:02:50,710 --> 00:02:52,909
AgriGenesis AI, always real data:

39
00:02:52,929 --> 00:02:58,220
from “I have land but no idea” to “I know where to start”. Thank you!
